[00:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The Dyson CameraJet™. A toothbrush that didn\'t start as one. Where did it start? Brushing? Nope. A jet, because jets can floss. Brushes can\'t. The jet worked.'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Great. Great needed to be better. More better. A conical jet that does this… not this. Except we needed it faster. Double faster.'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So fast it fired one millisecond blasts. Apologies, chia seeds. But we noticed a few gaps you can\'t see. So we added a camera. Smaller, smaller, one millimetre to be precise.'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But it needed to film whilst vibrating. So, we upped the camera frame rate. More frames, 28 frames. Added an LED strobe light until shaky became steady. Chef\'s kiss.'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '"What if the camera misses a gap?" we thought. We rethought. Created a machine learning algorithm that thought for us. One developed on images of the mouth. More images, over 470,000 images.'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So it could see, predict and automatically recognise the gaps to clean. That was something to smile about. But what about behind the smile? We went deeper, studied plaque. Grew our own plaque.'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Keep your enemies close, right? We made mouthwash and toothpaste at the same time. Now there was an idea. Why not mouthwash at the same time you floss and brush? We did, using the exact recommended amount dispensed by the brush. By then we had a total oral care system and toothbrush –'

[01:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We forgot to talk about the brush… Oscillations. Variable oscillations. Anti-stalling. Better motor.'

[01:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A sonic motor. More oscillations, 58,000 a minute, then… we stopped. We had a toothbrush. Kind of.'

[01:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It felt wrong calling it one. Dyson CameraJet™.'
